# 18. One more data correctness bug: ALLOW ≠ WON

`LabProjector` currently does:

```text
gate ALLOW
→ if no external outcome
→ outcome = won
```

That will poison the Lab dataset.

A WorkerKit gate means:

> allowed to submit / allowed to perform irreversible action.

It does **not** mean:

> external bounty won.

You need distinct states:

```text
execution_status:
COMPLETED | FAILED

verification_status:
PASS | FAIL | UNKNOWN

commit_status:
ALLOWED | DENIED

submission_status:
SUBMITTED | NOT_SUBMITTED

external_outcome:
WON | LOST | PAID | REJECTED | UNKNOWN
```

Until an external outcome exists:

```text
external_outcome = UNKNOWN
```

Never infer it from a commit gate.

This matters enormously for your future analytics moat.

