# 19. Your evaluator needs a v2 before making learning claims

The multidimensional structure is good:

```text
requirement coverage
diversity
technical validity
specificity
novelty
rationale
```

But the scoring heuristics are extremely gameable.

For example novelty gets rewarded for mentioning existing products and words like:

```text
unlike
different from
```

and technical validity gets rewarded for mentioning:

```text
API
AWS
Docker
LLM
database
```

That means an agent can score better by keyword stuffing.

For the MVP evaluator use three independent channels:

```text
A. deterministic checks
   count, required sections, constraints, URLs, schema

B. pairwise judge
   v1 vs v2 blind comparison on rubric dimensions

C. adversarial reviewer
   identify concrete failure modes
```

Don't show the judge which output is v1/v2.

Shuffle ordering.

Run at least two judge passes with order reversed.

Store disagreement.

For the hackathon, that's enough.

