# 31. The canonical ETHOnline proof suite

I would replace P0–P10 with this stricter definition:

| Proof                    | PASS only when                                                                           |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **P0 Taxonomy**          | Same taxonomy hash appears in Oracle fixture → WorkOrder → RunCommitment → Lab           |
| **P1 Persistent Letta**  | Real `agent-*`/`agent-local-*`; 2+ fresh conversations; memory survives                  |
| **P2 WorkerVersion**     | Real MemFS Git commit + config/tool/skill digests generate WorkerVersion                 |
| **P3 WorkReceipt**       | Real Letta execution produced content-addressed artifact and valid WorkerKit event chain |
| **P4 Real TEE**          | `is_simulated == false`, real quote obtained                                             |
| **P5 TEE binding**       | External verifier confirms quote contains exact RunCommitment                            |
| **P6 Lease**             | Bob invokes real Worker under bounded lease; fourth/unauthorized call rejected           |
| **P7 Ethereum identity** | Real ERC-8004 identity exists on testnet with real registration metadata                 |
| **P8 Validation**        | Real validation links exact Worker + WorkReceipt/attestation                             |
| **P9 Experience reuse**  | Run B actually calls Lab context derived from Run A and records dependency               |
| **P10 Learning**         | Real v2 MemFS diff beats real v1 on blinded held-out A/B                                 |
| **P11 Reusable capital** | Real asset from prior Run is acquired and used by subsequent Run                         |
| **P12 ENSv2**            | Real worker subname resolves on Sepolia to current Worker/agent metadata                 |

**No simulator can satisfy P4.**

**No generated fake address can satisfy P7.**

**No manually-created artifact can satisfy P6.**

**No `DeterministicMockEvaluator` can satisfy P10.**

That's the rule.

